    "title": "TIFF 2026 - The Face of Horror Review - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Brendan Frye ,\n1 days ago I love the Midnight Madness program at TIFF because it gives festivalgoers some of the most outlandish and unique takes on film you can find at the festival. This is the same program that gave us Color Out of Space and Obsession, so it has led to some pretty interesting works, and this year’s The Face of Horror definitely fits into that category. Read full article",
